      "Somewhere in your head, the same conversation has been running on a loop for years, and it has never reached an ending because endings require witnesses.",
      "You know the conversation. You've made the case both ways. You've argued that this is a problem — listed the evidence, named the costs, looked at the data — and then, sometimes within the same hour, you've argued that it isn't. Other people have worse habits. You're functional. You can stop whenever. The argument is real on both sides, which is why it has lasted.",
