      "This is why the first honest sentence is the hardest sentence. It's not that telling someone makes them responsible for the outcome. They aren't, and they shouldn't be. It's that telling someone makes you unable to forget that you have been considering this seriously. The deferral is over. The deliberation, finally, has weight.",
