      "For some people, the honest answer is: it was permitting feelings I'm not allowed to have sober. Grief I cannot afford to fully feel. Anger I cannot direct at the people I'm actually angry at. A loneliness that has no acceptable outlet. The substance was where the feelings were allowed to come out the side door.",
      "The substance wasn't the addiction. The function was. The substance was just the cheapest provider.",
