      "For some people, the answer is: most of it was you, the substance was incidental, and the friendships are mostly going to hold. For other people, the answer is: a lot of it was the substance, and the social life is going to need to be partially rebuilt from scratch, on terms you haven't designed yet because you didn't know they would need designing.",
      "Both answers are survivable. Neither answer is fixable in a hurry.",
      "The mistake in early sobriety is treating the loneliness as an emergency. You go to too many meetings, you sign up for the gym and the running club and the language class, you over-invest in any new relationship that feels remotely warm. You are trying to outrun the silence. This rarely works. The substitute activities are not bad — some of them will be load-bearing later — but in the early months, they are mostly compensatory, and you can feel the compensation in them, and so can the people around you, and the new relationships have a slightly desperate quality that does not serve them.",
