      "What you're afraid of losing isn't fun. It's peaks.",
      "The fear is real. You've read the success stories — the people who got sober, found God or running or pottery, and now claim to be happier than they've ever been. You don't believe them. The version of yourself that has had the actual fun you're considering giving up cannot imagine that life will be anything but flat without it. You aren't being cynical. You're being honest. You've never lived the alternative. The substance has been the operating system of your social life for years, and you have no functioning frame of reference for what's underneath it.",
