      "This is the distinction that matters.",
      "Substance fun is vertical. It is a sharp spike of pleasure delivered in a tight window — three hours on a Friday night where everything is funny, everyone is interesting, the conversation is electric, and at some point in the evening you peak at a level of feeling-good that the rest of your week cannot match. The peak is real. It is also expensive. The cost is paid in the hangover, the Saturday lost to fog, the slow erosion of the rest of the week's ambient mood, and the increasing gap between how alive you feel inside the peak and how dead you feel outside it.",
